{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Credit Risk and Loan Default Prediction\n",
    "### Course: MBA Introduction to Python Programming\n",
    "**Methodology:** Multiple Logistic Regression with Balanced Class Weighting  \n",
    "**Dataset:** LendingClub Historical Accepted Loans (2007–2018 Q4)  \n",
    "**Target Variable:** Probability of Default ($PD \\in [0, 1]$)  \n",
    "**Institutional Framework:** Basel II/III Retail Internal Ratings-Based (IRB) Standards  \n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 1. Executive Summary & Academic Objectives\n",
    "In retail banking and fintech lending, evaluating credit risk is the cornerstone of capital adequacy and prudent risk management. When an applicant applies for an unsecured personal loan, the financial institution must accurately estimate their **Probability of Default (PD)** to support risk-based underwriting, interest rate pricing, and expected loss calculations:  \n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\text{Expected Loss (EL)} = \\text{PD} \\times \\text{LGD} \\times \\text{EAD}$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Where:\n",
    "- $\\text{PD}$: Probability of Default (the output of this econometric model)\n",
    "- $\\text{LGD}$: Loss Given Default (percentage lost after recoveries)\n",
    "- $\\text{EAD}$: Exposure at Default (total outstanding balance at default)\n",
    "\n",
    "### End-to-End Project Workflow\n",
    "```\n",
    "[ Phase 1: Ingest .csv.gz & Filter Resolved Loans ] \n",
    "                     │\n",
    "                     ▼\n",
    "[ Phase 2: Feature Engineering (LTI) & Median Imputation ] \n",
    "                     │\n",
    "                     ▼\n",
    "[ Phase 3: Exploratory Data Analysis & Risk Driver Profiling ] \n",
    "                     │\n",
    "                     ▼\n",
    "[ Phase 4: Stratified 80/20 Split & Balanced Logistic Regression ] \n",
    "                     │\n",
    "                     ▼\n",
    "[ Phase 5: Calibrated Credit Risk Grading (A to F) ] \n",
    "                     │\n",
    "                     ▼\n",
    "[ Phase 6: Model Serialization & Streamlit Underwriting UI ]\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Phase 1: Dataset Inspection & Data Hygiene\n",
    "We read directly from the compressed archive `accepted_2007_to_2018Q4.csv.gz` using memory-efficient reading methods (`usecols`)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "import gzip\n",
    "import math\n",
    "import json\n",
    "import pickle\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "\n",
    "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
    "from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import (\n",
    "    roc_auc_score,\n",
    "    roc_curve,\n",
    "    confusion_matrix,\n",
    "    classification_report,\n",
    "    precision_recall_curve\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "sns.set_theme(style=\"whitegrid\", palette=\"muted\")\n",
    "%matplotlib inline\n",
    "\n",
    "DATA_PATH = \"../data/accepted_2007_to_2018Q4.csv.gz\"\n",
    "if not os.path.exists(DATA_PATH):\n",
    "    DATA_PATH = \"data/accepted_2007_to_2018Q4.csv.gz\"\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Loading dataset from:\", DATA_PATH)\n",
    "use_cols = [\"id\", \"member_id\", \"loan_status\", \"annual_inc\", \"dti\", \"fico_range_low\", \"loan_amnt\"]\n",
    "df_raw = pd.read_csv(DATA_PATH, usecols=use_cols, low_memory=False)\n",
    "print(f\"Raw records loaded: {len(df_raw):,} rows × {len(df_raw.columns)} columns\")\n",
    "df_raw.head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Inspecting `loan_status` & Eliminating Look-Ahead Bias\n",
    "Why must we exclude `Current` and `In Grace Period` loans?\n",
    "1. **Look-Ahead Bias:** Active ongoing contracts have not reached terminal maturity. A borrower who is current today could default months from now.\n",
    "2. **Supervisory Standard:** Regulators require Probability of Default (PD) to be modeled strictly on **resolved loan contracts**:\n",
    "   - `Fully Paid` $\\longrightarrow 0$ (Safe / Performing)\n",
    "   - `Charged Off` or `Default` $\\longrightarrow 1$ (Credit Loss Event)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"Raw Loan Status Frequencies:\")\n",
    "display(df_raw[\"loan_status\"].value_counts())\n",
    "\n",
    "# Clean string formatting\n",
    "df_raw[\"loan_status\"] = df_raw[\"loan_status\"].astype(str).str.strip()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Filter resolved loans only\n",
    "resolved_mask = df_raw[\"loan_status\"].isin([\"Fully Paid\", \"Charged Off\", \"Default\"])\n",
    "df_clean = df_raw[resolved_mask].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Map binary target\n",
    "df_clean[\"target\"] = df_clean[\"loan_status\"].apply(lambda s: 0 if s == \"Fully Paid\" else 1)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Drop non-predictive identifiers\n",
    "df_clean.drop(columns=[\"id\", \"member_id\", \"loan_status\"], inplace=True, errors=\"ignore\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Retained {len(df_clean):,} resolved loan contracts.\")\n",
    "target_counts = df_clean[\"target\"].value_counts()\n",
    "print(f\"Safe (0): {target_counts[0]:,} ({target_counts[0]/len(df_clean)*100:.1f}%)\")\n",
    "print(f\"Default (1): {target_counts[1]:,} ({target_counts[1]/len(df_clean)*100:.1f}%)\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Phase 2: Feature Engineering & Preprocessing\n",
    "We calculate the **Loan-to-Income (LTI)** ratio:\n",
    "$$\\text{LTI} = \\frac{\\text{loan\\_amnt}}{\\text{annual\\_inc}}$$\n",
    "To prevent mathematical exceptions (such as division by zero) and stabilize regression coefficients, we enforce:\n",
    "- Flooring zero or negative incomes to \\$1,000.\n",
    "- Dropping rows with missing values in required predictors (complete-case analysis).\n",
    "- Clipping extreme 99.5th percentile outliers in `annual_inc` and `dti`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 1. Median Imputation for DTI\n",
    "dti_median = df_clean[\"dti\"].median()\n",
    "df_clean[\"dti\"] = df_clean[\"dti\"].fillna(dti_median)\n",
    "\n",
    "# 2. Division-by-Zero Protection on Income\n",
    "df_clean[\"annual_inc\"] = df_clean[\"annual_inc\"].apply(lambda inc: max(1000.0, float(inc)))\n",
    "\n",
    "# 3. Outlier Winsorization / Clipping\n",
    "inc_cap = df_clean[\"annual_inc\"].quantile(0.995)\n",
    "df_clean[\"annual_inc\"] = np.clip(df_clean[\"annual_inc\"], a_min=1000.0, a_max=inc_cap)\n",
    "df_clean[\"dti\"] = np.clip(df_clean[\"dti\"], a_min=0.0, a_max=45.0)\n",
    "\n",
    "# 4. Feature Engineering: LTI\n",
    "df_clean[\"LTI\"] = (df_clean[\"loan_amnt\"] / df_clean[\"annual_inc\"]).clip(0.0, 1.5)\n",
    "\n",
    "FEATURES = [\"annual_inc\", \"dti\", \"fico_range_low\", \"loan_amnt\", \"LTI\"]\n",
    "print(\"Engineered Predictors:\", FEATURES)\n",
    "df_clean[FEATURES].describe()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Phase 3: Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)\n",
    "We analyze risk patterns across FICO, DTI, Loan Amount, and Leverage."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 2, figsize=(14, 10))\n",
    "\n",
    "# 1. Outcome Distribution\n",
    "sns.countplot(data=df_clean, x=\"target\", ax=axes[0, 0], palette=[\"#218C87\", \"#C94C4C\"])\n",
    "axes[0, 0].set_title(\"Loan Outcome Distribution (0=Paid, 1=Default)\", fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "axes[0, 0].set_xticklabels([\"Fully Paid (0)\", \"Default / Charged Off (1)\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "# 2. FICO vs Default\n",
    "fico_bins = pd.cut(df_clean[\"fico_range_low\"], bins=[600, 660, 700, 740, 780, 850])\n",
    "df_clean.groupby(fico_bins)[\"target\"].mean().plot(kind=\"bar\", ax=axes[0, 1], color=\"#537895\")\n",
    "axes[0, 1].set_title(\"Default Rate by FICO Score Band\", fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "axes[0, 1].set_ylabel(\"Observed Default Rate\")\n",
    "axes[0, 1].tick_params(axis=\"x\", rotation=25)\n",
    "\n",
    "# 3. DTI vs Default\n",
    "dti_bins = pd.cut(df_clean[\"dti\"], bins=[0, 10, 15, 20, 25, 30, 46])\n",
    "df_clean.groupby(dti_bins)[\"target\"].mean().plot(kind=\"bar\", ax=axes[1, 0], color=\"#D99A35\")\n",
    "axes[1, 0].set_title(\"Default Rate by Debt-to-Income (DTI) Band\", fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "axes[1, 0].set_ylabel(\"Observed Default Rate\")\n",
    "axes[1, 0].tick_params(axis=\"x\", rotation=25)\n",
    "\n",
    "# 4. Correlation Heatmap\n",
    "corr = df_clean[FEATURES + [\"target\"]].corr()\n",
    "sns.heatmap(corr, annot=True, fmt=\".2f\", cmap=\"RdBu_r\", ax=axes[1, 1], vmin=-1, vmax=1)\n",
    "axes[1, 1].set_title(\"Predictor Correlation Matrix\", fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Phase 4: Multiple Logistic Regression Model\n",
    "We partition the dataset into an **80/20 stratified split** and fit `StandardScaler` strictly on `X_train` to prevent **Data Leakage**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "X = df_clean[FEATURES]\n",
    "y = df_clean[\"target\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "# 80/20 Stratified Partitioning\n",
    "X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(\n",
    "    X, y, test_size=0.20, random_state=42, stratify=y\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Standardization: Fit on Train ONLY\n",
    "scaler = StandardScaler()\n",
    "scaler.fit(X_train)\n",
    "\n",
    "X_train_scaled = pd.DataFrame(scaler.transform(X_train), columns=FEATURES, index=X_train.index)\n",
    "X_test_scaled = pd.DataFrame(scaler.transform(X_test), columns=FEATURES, index=X_test.index)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Train Multiple Logistic Regression with balanced weighting\n",
    "clf = LogisticRegression(class_weight=\"balanced\", random_state=42, max_iter=1000)\n",
    "clf.fit(X_train_scaled, y_train)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Model Fitting Complete!\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Econometric Coefficients & Odds Ratios ($e^\\beta$)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "coef_df = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    \"Feature\": FEATURES,\n",
    "    \"Beta (Standardized)\": clf.coef_[0],\n",
    "    \"Odds Ratio (e^Beta)\": np.exp(clf.coef_[0])\n",
    "})\n",
    "coef_df[\"Interpretation\"] = coef_df.apply(\n",
    "    lambda r: f\"1-SD increase {'cuts' if r['Beta (Standardized)'] < 0 else 'increases'} default odds by {abs(r['Odds Ratio (e^Beta)']-1)*100:.1f}%.\",\n",
    "    axis=1\n",
    ")\n",
    "display(coef_df)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Test Set Evaluation: ROC-AUC, Precision, Recall & Confusion Matrix"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "y_prob = clf.predict_proba(X_test_scaled)[:, 1]\n",
    "y_pred = clf.predict(X_test_scaled)\n",
    "\n",
    "auc_score = roc_auc_score(y_test, y_prob)\n",
    "print(f\"Holdout Test ROC-AUC Score: {auc_score:.4f}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nClassification Report (0.50 Threshold):\\n\")\n",
    "print(classification_report(y_test, y_pred, target_names=[\"Safe (0)\", \"Default (1)\"]))\n",
    "\n",
    "cm = confusion_matrix(y_test, y_pred)\n",
    "print(\"Confusion Matrix:\\n\", cm)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Phase 5: Calibrated Credit Risk Grading (A to F)\n",
    "We assign credit grades based on the model's predicted probability of default ($PD$) and verify monotonic risk ranking."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "GRADE_CUTOFFS = {\n",
    "    \"A\": 0.32,\n",
    "    \"B\": 0.44,\n",
    "    \"C\": 0.54,\n",
    "    \"D\": 0.64,\n",
    "    \"E\": 0.74,\n",
    "    \"F\": 1.00\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "def assign_grade(pd_val):\n",
    "    if pd_val < GRADE_CUTOFFS[\"A\"]: return \"A\"\n",
    "    elif pd_val < GRADE_CUTOFFS[\"B\"]: return \"B\"\n",
    "    elif pd_val < GRADE_CUTOFFS[\"C\"]: return \"C\"\n",
    "    elif pd_val < GRADE_CUTOFFS[\"D\"]: return \"D\"\n",
    "    elif pd_val < GRADE_CUTOFFS[\"E\"]: return \"E\"\n",
    "    else: return \"F\"\n",
    "\n",
    "test_df = pd.DataFrame({\"actual\": y_test.values, \"pd\": y_prob})\n",
    "test_df[\"grade\"] = test_df[\"pd\"].apply(assign_grade)\n",
    "\n",
    "grade_summary = test_df.groupby(\"grade\").agg(\n",
    "    applicant_count=(\"actual\", \"count\"),\n",
    "    avg_model_pd=(\"pd\", \"mean\"),\n",
    "    actual_default_rate=(\"actual\", \"mean\")\n",
    ").reindex([\"A\", \"B\", \"C\", \"D\", \"E\", \"F\"]).fillna(0)\n",
    "\n",
    "grade_summary[\"portfolio_share_pct\"] = (grade_summary[\"applicant_count\"] / len(test_df)) * 100\n",
    "display(grade_summary)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Phase 6: Single Applicant Underwriting Function"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def assess_borrower(annual_inc: float, dti: float, fico: float, loan_amnt: float):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Scores an individual loan applicant using the trained pipeline.\"\"\"\n",
    "    inc = max(1000.0, annual_inc)\n",
    "    lti = min(1.5, loan_amnt / inc)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    raw = pd.DataFrame([{\n",
    "        \"annual_inc\": inc,\n",
    "        \"dti\": min(45.0, dti),\n",
    "        \"fico_range_low\": fico,\n",
    "        \"loan_amnt\": loan_amnt,\n",
    "        \"LTI\": lti\n",
    "    }])[FEATURES]\n",
    "    \n",
    "    scaled = scaler.transform(raw)\n",
    "    pd_score = float(clf.predict_proba(scaled)[0, 1])\n",
    "    grade = assign_grade(pd_score)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    return {\n",
    "        \"Probability of Default\": f\"{pd_score*100:.2f}%\ theater\",\n",
    "        \"Credit Grade\": f\"Grade {grade}\",\n",
    "        \"Derived LTI\": f\"{lti:.3f}\",\n",
    "        \"Recommendation\": \"Approved\" if grade in [\"A\", \"B\", \"C\", \"D\"] else \"Manual Review / Decline\"\n",
    "    }\n",
    "\n",
    "sample_borrower = assess_borrower(annual_inc=85000, dti=14.2, fico=740, loan_amnt=12000)\n",
    "print(\"Sample Underwriting Result:\", sample_borrower)"
   ]
  }
 ],
